+# Coupled run status
+
+Use the native command to inspect an existing coupled run without making provider
+calls, running tools, or changing the run directory:
+
+```text
+spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+`PATH` is resolved relative to the caller's current working directory. The
+installed npm entry forwards the same command and arguments:
+
+```text
+npx spiral-coder coupled-status --run-dir PATH
+```
+
+The command reads `iterations.json` and each native `state/tui-work.json`
+ledger. `wire_requests` counts every durable request in `requests`;
+`task_requests` counts requests charged to `task` (including the native default
+when charge is omitted). Failed and in-flight attempts therefore count too.
+Text logs and report prose are not used.
+
+An interrupted run may lack its pending ledger. In that case pending usage and
+the aggregate used and remaining values are `null`, not zero. Limits remain
+known. A pending ledger that exists must be valid. The reported `completed`
+status is the recorded native manifest state; it is not an independent
+verification or promotion authorization.
+
+The following is the completed synthetic example from
+`scripts.status_fixture.make` and equals `scripts.status_fixture.expected('completed')`:
+
+```json
+{"version":1,"status":"completed","stop_reason":"completed","iterations":[{"iteration":1,"task_id":"t1","termination":"completed","task_requests":2,"wire_requests":3,"changed_files":["src/a.rs"],"newly_verified":["cargo test -q"]}],"pending":null,"requests":{"task_used":2,"wire_used":3,"task_limit":192,"wire_limit":216,"task_remaining":190,"wire_remaining":213}}
+```
